        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "721f5675-11a1-552a-8747-af000a2be32d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Hoffmann, Paul von Hindenburg, Erich Ludendorff\n- Events: Battle of Tannenberg, Masurian Lakes, Battle of Liège, Treaty of Brest-Litovsk, Polish–Soviet War in 1919\n- Roles: German general, commander of German forces in the east, chief negotiator\n\nFacts:\n- Erich Ludendorff was a German general who lived from 9 April 1865 to 20 December 1937.\n- Erich Ludendorff was the victor of the Battle of Liège and the Battle of Tannenberg.\n- Max Hoffmann, together with Paul von Hindenburg and Erich Ludendorff, masterminded the defeat of the Russian armies at Tannenberg and the Masurian Lakes.\n- During the period of the Polish–Soviet War in 1919, Max Hoffmann commanded the German forces in the east.\n- Max Hoffmann was also a chief negotiator in the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk.\n- During the period of the Polish–Soviet War in 1919, Max Hoffmann was facing increasing difficulties.",
